330: not an inferred deformation of complex quotients.
331: 
332: For a=1 the z-only auxiliary weight is zero. The same formula does not
333: give a locally free auxiliary quotient there, and RT.8 makes no assertion
334: about that different stratum. Also, a contracting factor containing q can
335: send a fixed-coordinate level to an infinite or collapsed end as q tends
336: to zero. The actual adjacent node-chart reindex is still required before
337: the two finite ends of this cut can be glued by B. That reindex and its
338: labelled outer-fan map remain the two gates in RT.7.
339: 
340: ## RT.9. The reduced link and its framed fixed three-sphere
341: 
342: The actual positive quotient of RT.8 is
343: \[
344:  W=\operatorname{Tot}\bigl(O(-1)\oplus O(-2)\longrightarrow
345:  \mathbb P^2_{[S_0:S_1:z]}\bigr),
346: \]
347: with fibre coordinates T1,V: on the three nonzero homogeneous-coordinate
348: charts, the auxiliary coefficient transition functions are their first
349: and second inverse powers. The physical action is z of weight one and V
350: of weight minus one. Its fixed surface is F=D(O(-1) over P1), and its
351: other fixed point is [0:0:1] with zero fibre coordinates.
352: 
353: The disk-bundle boundary L=S(O(-1) plus O(-2)) has integral groups
354: H2=Z,H4=Z/2,H5=Z. Indeed the sphere-bundle Gysin Euler map from H0(CP2)
355: to H4(CP2) is multiplication by two. The adjacent exact terms give the
356: other groups. Thus this link is not substituted for a homotopy sphere.
357: The disk bundle is spin, since c1=3h-h-2h=0; its middle form is [2]
358: and p1=3h2+(h2+4h2)=8h2.
359: 
360: On F set R=||S|| |T1|. At R=epsilon, take the unique positive auxiliary
361: gauge ||S||=1 and write T1=epsilon exp(i phi). Then
362: \[
363:                   p=e^{i\varphi}(S_0,S_1)\in S^3
364: \]
365: is invariant under the remaining auxiliary circle and is the actual
366: fixed-set boundary map. The positive-weight normal coefficients have
367: the exact arrow
368: \[
369:  (z,\overline V)\longmapsto
370:  (e^{i(a-1)\varphi}z,e^{ia\varphi}\overline V).       \tag{RT.9}
371: \]
372: Before the positive gauge, the second coordinate also carries the
373: positive factor ||S||^(2a); it is retained in the real quotient map.
374: The physical action is scalar on both displayed coefficients. Its
375: original complex normal orientation is the negative of this spinor
376: orientation, because precisely V was conjugated.
377: 
378: The finite free-end map is also explicit. In the common Cox line xi
379: of auxiliary weight a, put Nt=|xi| ||t||^a, Ns=|xi|/||s||^a and
380: R=||s|| ||t||. Since Nt=R^a Ns, the map Nt=1 to Ns=1 is
381: \[
382:  (\xi,\xi_{\rm dual})\longmapsto
383:  (R^a\xi,R^{-a}\xi_{\rm dual}),\qquad\xi\xi_{\rm dual}=q.
384:                                                         \tag{RT.10}
385: \]
386: It is smooth and bounded on R>=epsilon, preserves q, and extends both
387: q=0 branches. Auxiliary normalization is performed afterward. The q
388: factor in B is first absorbed in the actual adjacent node charts
389: \[
390:  U_j=\frac{w}{(2\lambda)^jq^j},\quad
391:  V_j=\frac{(2\lambda)^jq^{j+1}}w,\quad
392:  B:(j,U_j,V_j)\mapsto(j+1,\rho U_j,\rho^{-1}V_j).
393: \]
394: The Cartier coefficient rho is the identity in the common Cox line.
395: This is an arrow between node charts, not a limit of q-scaling on one
396: chart. The fixed S3 in (RT.9) remains on the inner end. That end is
397: therefore not identified with the bare ruling mapping torus of RT.5.
398: 
399: ## RT.10. A specified local fixed-sphere surgery and its physical line
400: 
401: Attach D4 times D4 to the reduced disk bundle W along its fixed
402: S3 times D4 tube using (RT.9). The circle is trivial on the first
403: factor and has the original normal weights (+1,-1) on the second.
404: This is an explicit equivariant handle attachment. Its boundary Y
405: has free circle action. The capped fixed surface is CP2 with reversed
406: orientation, with exceptional generator E squared equal to minus one;
407: the separate charge-one point is unchanged.
408: 
409: The normal line direction follows from the actual ideal inclusion:
410: O(-E) has inside frame T1, so an inside coefficient c becomes T1*c
411: in the outside trivial line. Hence (RT.9) extends the positive spinor as
412: \[
413:  \mathcal E=O(-(a-1)E)\oplus O(-aE),\quad
414:  c_1(\mathcal E)=(1-2a)E,\quad c_2(\mathcal E)=-a(a-1),
415:  \quad p_1(\operatorname{ad}\mathcal E)=-1.             \tag{RT.11}
416: \]
417: Here a=2 in the reduced disk bundle. The same polynomial records the
418: displayed framed-surface calculation for other integer charges.
419: 
420: Here O(kE) denotes the smooth complex line with its displayed clutch;
421: no complex structure on the capped reversed CP2 is asserted.
422: Orient BF=P(Ecal) by the orientation inherited from complex F and
423: extended across its cap, followed by the complex projective fibre,
424: and set h=c1(O(1)).
425: The projective coefficient sequence gives
426: h2+c1(Ecal)h+c2(Ecal)=0 and pi_*h=1. The physical line is M=O(-1).
427: Its two separate characteristic integrals are therefore
428: \[
429:  (k_{B_F},\ell_{B_F})=(3a^2-3a+1,4).                 \tag{RT.12}
430: \]
431: Indeed pi_*h3=c1(Ecal)^2-c2(Ecal)=-3a2+3a-1. The vertical tangent
432: class is 2h+c1(Ecal), whose squared pushforward is
433: c1(Ecal)^2-4c2(Ecal)=-1; the base p1 integral is -3. Dualizing h
434: gives exactly the physical signs in (RT.12).
435: 
436: We retain the three actual boundary orientations. The positive-spinor
437: polar orientation is dr wedge ddelta wedge Omega_CP1. Conjugating V
438: reverses that normal real4 orientation. The circle-first orbit
439: orientation near the fixed surface is consequently
440: Omega_F wedge dr wedge Omega_CP1. Its deleted tube contributes -BF.
441: At the other fixed point the weights are (-1,-1,+1,+1); conjugating
442: two coordinates preserves real8 orientation, and its deleted ball
443: contributes positive complex CP3, with physical line O(-1). At the
444: outside, moving the circle past the outward normal contributes
445: minus the physical quotient Y/S1. Thus the free quotient bordism has
446: \[
447:           \partial Q=-Y/S^1\;\sqcup\;-B_F\;\sqcup\;\mathbb P^3.
448:                                                         \tag{RT.13}
449: \]
450: On CP3 the physical integrals are (-1,-4). The associated physical
451: line extends over Q. The stable tangent bundle of its free total
452: space is the orbit tangent plus the trivial circle direction, so p1
453: also extends. Stokes, using product connections on every collar,
454: gives, for the reduced a=2 model,
455: \[
456:  (k_{Y/S^1},\ell_{Y/S^1})=(-8,-8),\qquad
457:                  (4k-\ell)/24=-1.                    \tag{RT.14}
458: \]
459: This computes the specified framed local surgery boundary Y. It does
460: not identify Y, its orientation, or its line/cap marking with the
461: unassembled residual end of the global source-zero family. That
462: labelled attachment, including the j=-1 versus requested node fan,
463: remains open. No individual source-zero return is assigned here.
